---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const meta = {
  category: 'Systems & Automation',
  tags:     ['Python', 'Flask', 'SQLite', 'Internal Tooling'],
  readTime: '6 min read',
};

const tickets = [
  { id: '001', reporter: 'Legal Asst. A', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Printer Jam / Paper Feed',         priority: 'Medium', status: 'Resolved',    days: '1' },
  { id: '002', reporter: 'Legal Asst. B', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Printer Offline – Network',        priority: 'High',   status: 'Resolved',    days: '2' },
  { id: '003', reporter: 'Admin A',        dept: 'Administration',   issue: 'Software Login Issue',             priority: 'Medium', status: 'Resolved',    days: '1' },
  { id: '004', reporter: 'Legal Asst. C', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Printer Ink / Toner Empty',        priority: 'Low',    status: 'Resolved',    days: '3' },
  { id: '005', reporter: 'Legal Asst. A', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Training – Document Management',   priority: 'Medium', status: 'In Progress', days: '—' },
  { id: '006', reporter: 'Admin B',        dept: 'Administration',   issue: 'Training – New Software Rollout', priority: 'High',   status: 'Resolved',    days: '4' },
  { id: '007', reporter: 'Legal Asst. D', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Printer Jam / Paper Feed',         priority: 'Medium', status: 'Resolved',    days: '1' },
  { id: '008', reporter: 'Legal Asst. B', dept: 'Legal Assistants', issue: 'Training – Workflow Process',      priority: 'Low',    status: 'Open',        days: '—' },
];
---

<Layout title="When Nobody Owns IT">

<!-- ── ARTICLE HERO ── -->
<section class="art-hero">
  <div class="art-hero-grid"></div>
  <div class="art-hero-glow"></div>
  <div class="art-hero-inner">

    <a href="/work" class="back-link fade-up d1">← Back to Work</a>

    <div class="art-eyebrow fade-up d2">// {meta.category}</div>
    <h1 class="art-headline fade-up d3">
      When Nobody<br>Owns <em>IT</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="art-subheadline fade-up d4">
      Building a Triage System for a Professional Office
    </p>

    <div class="art-meta fade-up d5">
      <div class="art-tags">
        {meta.tags.map((t) => <span class="tag">{t}</span>)}
      </div>
      <span class="art-read-time">{meta.readTime}</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── ARTICLE BODY ── -->
<div class="art-body-wrap">
  <article class="art-body">

    <!-- 01 The Situation -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">01</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">The Situation</h2>
      <p>
        The office has 18 staff, one IT contract vendor called in for major failures,
        and no internal system for anything smaller. When a printer jams or a workstation
        loses network access, the resolution path is: notice it, mention it to whoever
        is nearby, hope they mention it to someone with the credentials to fix it.
        Sometimes that chain works in an hour. Sometimes it takes three days.
      </p>
      <p>
        I came in as a coordinator and watched this happen a dozen times before I started
        keeping notes. The notes revealed the problem.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 The Problem -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">02</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">The Problem with Reactive IT</h2>
      <p>
        Without a log, every issue looks like a one-off. The printer jammed again —
        but "again" exists only in people's heads, and people's heads disagree on how
        often "again" actually is. There's no timestamp, no resolution path, no record
        of whether the same machine failed in the same way two weeks ago.
      </p>
      <p>
        The practical consequence: you can't prioritize by impact because you don't
        know impact. You can't make the case for replacing a failing printer because
        you can't demonstrate the load it creates. You can't identify whether a "training
        issue" is an isolated knowledge gap or a rollout that nobody fully understood.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every systemic problem stays invisible because the only data you have is anecdotal.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 The Approach -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">03</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">The Approach</h2>
      <p>
        I built IT Logger — a lightweight internal ticket system designed to answer one
        question: where is IT time actually going?
      </p>
      <p>
        The requirements were deliberately minimal. No ticket queue, no SLA tracking,
        no ITIL compliance. Just: who reported it, what department, what type of issue,
        what priority, when it was logged, and when it was closed. Everything runs
        locally — Python backend, Flask for the UI, SQLite for storage. No external
        dependencies, no licensing costs, no learning curve.
      </p>
      <p>
        The harder problem was adoption. A system nobody uses is just documentation debt.
        I designed the intake form to take under two minutes, with a small dropdown set
        for issue type that forced categorization without creating friction. Staff could
        self-report or I could log on their behalf. Either path worked.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 What the Data Showed -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">04</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">What the Data Showed</h2>
      <p>
        After three months of logging, the distribution was clear enough to act on.
        Below is a sample from the ticket log — names anonymized, issue types cleaned
        up but representative of the real breakdown.
      </p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="ticket-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>#</th>
              <th>Reported By</th>
              <th>Department</th>
              <th>Issue Type</th>
              <th>Priority</th>
              <th>Status</th>
              <th>Days</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {tickets.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="mono">{t.id}</td>
                <td>{t.reporter}</td>
                <td>{t.dept}</td>
                <td>{t.issue}</td>
                <td>
                  <span class:list={['priority-badge', `priority-${t.priority.toLowerCase()}`]}>
                    {t.priority}
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <span class:list={['status-badge', `status-${t.status.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-')}`]}>
                    {t.status}
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td class="mono">{t.days}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 The Pattern -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">05</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">The Pattern</h2>
      <p>
        Printer issues account for the largest single category of IT load in the office,
        and they concentrate almost entirely in the Legal Assistants department — a group
        with high document throughput and shared hardware.
      </p>
      <p>
        What looked like random friction was a systemic gap. The same two printers
        appeared repeatedly. One was past its rated duty cycle. The other was a network
        printer with a configuration that disconnected under a specific set of conditions —
        conditions that occurred daily.
      </p>
      <p>
        The training issues told a parallel story. They weren't random knowledge gaps.
        They clustered around a document management software rollout that had happened
        six months earlier without a structured handoff. People had built their own
        workarounds, and those workarounds didn't match the system's design.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 The Outcome -->
    <section class="art-section">
      <div class="art-section-num">06</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">The Outcome</h2>
      <p>
        Visibility. That's the whole outcome, and it's enough.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before the triage system, leadership had a vague sense that IT issues were a
        time sink. After three months, they had a dashboard: issue volume by type,
        by department, by priority, by resolution time. Printer-related issues were
        consuming roughly 40% of logged IT time. The two highest-volume machines
        were both past their recommended replacement window.
      </p>
      <p>
        One printer was replaced. A 90-minute training refresher was scheduled for
        the document management system. Two recurring issue types dropped off the log
        entirely. The contract IT vendor now gets a summary report before each visit
        instead of starting every call from scratch.
      </p>

      <div class="outcome-stats">
        <div class="outcome-stat">
          <div class="outcome-val">40%</div>
          <div class="outcome-label">of IT time was printer-related</div>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-divider"></div>
        <div class="outcome-stat">
          <div class="outcome-val">&lt;2 min</div>
          <div class="outcome-label">to log each ticket</div>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-divider"></div>
        <div class="outcome-stat">
          <div class="outcome-val">$0</div>
          <div class="outcome-label">ongoing operating cost</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 What This Means for Your Business -->
    <section class="art-section art-section--last">
      <div class="art-section-num">07</div>
      <h2 class="art-section-heading">What This Means for Your Business</h2>
      <p>
        If you run a small professional office — law, accounting, consulting, medical
        admin — you almost certainly have a version of this problem. Not an IT crisis.
        Just an IT blind spot.
      </p>
      <p>
        The issues are getting handled. They're just not being counted, which means
        they're not being learned from. A lightweight logging system doesn't require
        a dedicated IT person. It requires someone willing to spend two minutes per
        ticket and a few hours building the thing.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's it. The compound value comes from the log, not from any individual ticket.
      </p>
    </section>

  </article>
</div>

<!-- ── CTA ── -->
<div class="cta-strip">
  <div class="cta-glow"></div>
  <div class="cta-eyebrow">// Have a Similar Problem?</div>
  <h2 class="cta-headline">Let's Build<br><em>Something That Sticks.</em></h2>
  <p class="cta-sub">
    Discovery calls are free and take 30 minutes. Come with a problem —
    leave knowing whether I'm the right fit to solve it.
  </p>
  <div class="cta-actions">
    <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Start a Conversation</a>
    <a href="/work" class="btn-ghost">More Write-Ups</a>
  </div>
</div>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── HERO ── */
  .art-hero {
    padding-top: var(--nav-h);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .art-hero-grid {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 60px 60px;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 90% 80% at 50% 50%, black 20%, transparent 100%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .art-hero-glow {
    position: absolute; top: -10%; right: 5%;
    width: 700px; height: 600px;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse, rgba(232,146,10,0.05) 0%, transparent 65%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .art-hero-inner {
    position: relative; z-index: 2;
    max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 48px 72px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted2); text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .art-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .art-headline {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(52px, 7vw, 88px);
    line-height: 0.9; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .art-headline em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); }
  .art-subheadline {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 28px);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .art-meta {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .art-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .art-read-time {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted2);
  }

  /* ── ARTICLE BODY ── */
  .art-body-wrap {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0 48px;
  }
  .art-body {
    max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 80px 0 100px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-left: 48px;
  }

  /* ── SECTIONS ── */
  .art-section {
    margin-bottom: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .art-section--last {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .art-section-num {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .art-section-heading {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 40px);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 28px; line-height: 1;
  }

  .art-section p {
    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .art-section p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── TABLE ── */
  .table-wrap {
    margin-top: 36px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border2);
  }
  .ticket-table {
    width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .ticket-table thead tr {
    background: var(--bg4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border2);
  }
  .ticket-table th {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .ticket-table tbody tr {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg3);
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .ticket-table tbody tr:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .ticket-table tbody tr:hover { background: var(--bg4); }
  .ticket-table td {
    padding: 11px 16px;
    color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .ticket-table td.mono {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 10px; color: var(--muted2);
  }

  /* Priority badges */
  .priority-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid;
  }
  .priority-high   { color: #f87171; border-color: rgba(248,113,113,0.3); background: rgba(248,113,113,0.07); }
  .priority-medium { color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--adim3); background: var(--adim); }
  .priority-low    { color: var(--muted2); border-color: var(--border2); background: transparent; }

  /* Status badges */
  .status-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid;
  }
  .status-resolved    { color: #4ade80; border-color: rgba(74,222,128,0.25); background: rgba(74,222,128,0.07); }
  .status-in-progress { color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--adim3); background: var(--adim); }
  .status-open        { color: var(--muted2); border-color: var(--border2); background: transparent; }

  /* ── OUTCOME STATS ── */
  .outcome-stats {
    display: flex; align-items: stretch;
    border: 1px solid var(--border2);
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .outcome-stat {
    flex: 1; padding: 24px 28px;
  }
  .outcome-val {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 36px;
    color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .outcome-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted2); line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .outcome-divider {
    width: 1px; background: var(--border2); flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* ── CTA STRIP ── */
  .cta-strip {
    padding: 100px 48px; text-align: center;
    position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--bg);
  }
  .cta-glow {
    position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: 800px; height: 400px;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse, rgba(232,146,10,0.06) 0%, transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .cta-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 20px; position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }
  .cta-headline {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 68px);
    line-height: 0.92; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 20px; position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }
  .cta-headline em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); display: block; }
  .cta-sub {
    font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 44px;
    max-width: 440px; margin-inline: auto; line-height: 1.7;
    position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }
  .cta-actions {
    display: flex; gap: 16px; justify-content: center;
    align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }

  /* ── RESPONSIVE ── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .art-hero-inner { padding: 48px 24px 56px; }
    .art-body-wrap  { padding: 0 24px; }
    .art-body       { padding: 60px 0 80px; padding-left: 24px; }
    .cta-strip      { padding: 80px 24px; }
    .outcome-stats  { flex-direction: column; }
    .outcome-divider { width: 100%; height: 1px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .art-body { border-left: none; padding-left: 0; }
    .table-wrap { border-left: none; border-right: none; margin-left: -24px; margin-right: -24px; }
  }
</style>
